{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The furthest position on this player’s timeline a seek will actually STICK on live"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"content, in seconds — the engine pulls back anything closer to the live edge."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" when it cannot say, and on non-live content."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["iOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maxLiveSeekPosition","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","text":"Double","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"? { ","kind":"text"},{"text":"get","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is safe: the SDK then does not clamp. Never guess — a guessed holdback could","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"place content worse than not clamping at all.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Why it exists: every engine enforces a minimum live offset it will not let playback","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sit inside. Seek past it and the engine quietly pulls back, so a target computed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"without it is a request the player is free to ignore.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Computed engine-side: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"currentTime + currentLiveOffset - minimumOffset"},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AVPlayerAdapter"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"returns nil and lets "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/optiviewadscore.OptiViewAdsCore\/documentation\/OptiViewAdsCore\/PlayerAdapter\/seekableEnd","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" bound the clamp on its own: AVFoundation’s live-offset"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"values describe where to POSITION live playback, not where a seek lands, and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"configuredTimeOffsetFromLive"},{"type":"text","text":" that looks like an integrator’s choice is populated from the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"playlist’s hold-back."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Defaulted to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" for the same reason as "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/optiviewadscore.OptiViewAdsCore\/documentation\/OptiViewAdsCore\/PlayerAdapter\/supportsParallelBuffering","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":": this"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"protocol is public and Swift has no optional members, so an integrator’s own"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"adapter must keep compiling."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"title":"maxLiveSeekPosition","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"property","modules":[{"name":"OptiViewAdsCore"}],"fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maxLiveSeekPosition","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","text":"Double","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"extendedModule":"OptiViewAdsCore","externalID":"s:15OptiViewAdsCore13PlayerAdapterPAAE19maxLiveSeekPositionSdSgvp","roleHeading":"Instance Property"},"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/optiviewadscore.OptiViewAdsCore\/documentation\/OptiViewAdsCore\/PlayerAdapter\/maxLiveSeekPosition-198sh","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/optiviewadscore.OptiViewAdsCore\/documentation\/OptiViewAdsCore","doc:\/\/optiviewadscore.OptiViewAdsCore\/documentation\/OptiViewAdsCore\/PlayerAdapter"]]}